\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3d\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_14\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(170.497225 43.424615) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_15\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(253.262775 29.412308) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" d=\"M 3187 4467 L 3187 3994 L 1229 3994 L 1101 2291 L 1146 2291 Q 1254 2445 1376 2553 Q 1498 2662 1664 2723 Q 1830 2784 2061 2784 Q 2445 2784 2745 2617 Q 3046 2451 3219 2144 Q 3392 1837 3392 1402 Q 3392 966 3213 633 Q 3034 301 2698 112 Q 2362 -77 1888 -77 Q 1517 -77 1254 35 Q 992 147 809 320 Q 627 493 493 685 L 896 992 Q 1069 730 1277 566 Q 1485 403 1888 403 Q 2342 403 2582 646 Q 2822 890 2822 1331 L 2822 1395 Q 2822 1837 2582 2080 Q 2342 2323 1888 2323 Q 1581 2323 1405 2211 Q 1229 2099 1088 1946 L 634 2010 L 794 4467 L 3187 4467 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_16\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(336.028325 34.083077) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p6bf9a96d73\"><rect x=\"46.1\" y=\"11.528\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Station speed (cases per hour)","note":null},"answer":"<p>The filler is slowest at 100 cases an hour: 100 × 3,800 = 380k cases a year. After 97% yield: <b>368.6k</b>.</p> <p>Demand is 400k, so Riverbend loses about <b>31.4k cases</b> a year: $126k of contribution.</p>"},{"q":"The upgrade makes the filler 17% faster. What happens?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Filler: 100 × 1.17 = 117 an hour. Now the <b>packer (110/hour) is the bottleneck</b>: 110 × 3,800 × 97% = 405.5k good cases, more than demand, so Riverbend can supply all 400k.</p> <p>Extra cases: 31.4k × $4 = <b>$126k a year</b>. Payback: $230k ÷ $126k = <b>1.8 years</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> a good investment, and the new bottleneck still leaves headroom above demand.</p>"},{"q":"Is there a cheaper way to get the same output?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Run the filler through breaks</b> with a relief operator: a few more hours a day on the bottleneck only</li> <li><b>Cut changeover time</b> between bottle sizes on the filler</li><li><b>Weekend shift</b> for the filler with a small buffer of filled bottles</li></ul> <p>These could close part of the gap within weeks; the upgrade is the durable fix.</p>"}],"reco":"Approve the filler upgrade. The filler is the bottleneck today, limiting output to about 368.6k good cases against 400k demand. Making it 17% faster moves the bottleneck to the packer, which still has enough capacity to meet demand, adding about $126k of contribution a year and paying back in 1.8 years. Meanwhile, run the filler through breaks to recover some volume now. Risk: faster filling could raise reject rates. Next step: trial the upgrade's speed on one product before committing.","great":["Finds the bottleneck from station speeds","Checks what becomes the bottleneck after the upgrade","Caps output at demand","Suggests quick wins on the bottleneck itself"],"id":47,"slug":"riverbend-bottling"}